---
import "../styles/root.css";
import Preview from "../components/1/preview.astro";
import bannerLight from "../assets/bayphl-banner-light.svg";
import bannerDark from "../assets/bayphl-banner-dark.svg";
import bannerVerticalDark from "../assets/bayphl-logo-vertical-dark.svg";
import bannerVerticalLight from "../assets/bayphl-logo-vertical-light.svg";
import FAQCardGrid from "../components/FAQCardGrid.astro";
import FAQCard from "../components/FAQCard.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Nunito:ital,wght@0,200..1000;1,200..1000&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="The Bay Area Puzzle Hunt League: A semi-regular series of in-person puzzle hunts taking place in the San Francisco Bay Area."
    />
    <title>BayPHL: The Bay Area Puzzle Hunt League</title>
    <style></style>
  </head>
  <body
    class="bg-cream dark:bg-smoke text-navy dark:text-cream min-h-dvh flex flex-col"
  >
    <div
      class="max-w-3xl lg:max-w-5xl min-h-dvh mx-auto dark:bg-earth bg-bayphl-white shadow-xl shadow-teal/10 flex flex-col"
    >
      <header
        class="gap-2 md:gap-6 flex flex-col items-center bg-linear-135 from-teal to-sage text-cream dark:color-navy py-4 mb-4"
      >
        <picture class="w-full px-[15%] h-auto mr-4">
          <source
            media={`(width < 768px) and (prefers-color-scheme: light)`}
            srcset={bannerVerticalDark.src}
            width={bannerVerticalDark.width}
            height={bannerVerticalDark.height}
          />
          <source
            media={`(width < 768px) and (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`}
            srcset={bannerVerticalLight.src}
            width={bannerVerticalLight.width}
            height={bannerVerticalLight.height}
          />
          <source
            media={`(prefers-color-scheme: dark)`}
            srcset={bannerLight.src}
            width={bannerLight.width}
            height={bannerLight.height}
          />
          <source
            srcset={bannerDark.src}
            width={bannerDark.width}
            height={bannerDark.height}
          />
          <img
            class="w-[185px] md:w-full mx-auto"
            src={bannerDark.src}
            width={bannerDark.width}
            height={bannerDark.height}
            alt="BayPHL"
          />
        </picture>
        <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-[2.5rem] font-bold tracking-wide">
          Bay Area Puzzle Hunt League
        </h1>
      </header>
      <main class="py-4 px-4 md:px-8">
        <h2 class="mt-0">Past Hunts</h2>

        <Preview />

        <h2>About BayPHL</h2>

        <p class="text-lg">
          BayPHL is the <strong>Bay Area Puzzle Hunt League</strong>, a
          semi-regularly recurring, in-person puzzle hunts taking place in the
          San Francisco Bay Area.
        </p>

        <FAQCardGrid>
          <FAQCard>
            <Fragment slot="title">What is a puzzle hunt?</Fragment>
            <Fragment slot="content">
              <p>
                A puzzle hunt is a game in which players solve a series of
                difficult puzzles that require various logical,
                lateral-thinking, and creative skills to solve. These puzzles
                often come without explicit instructions on how to solve them,
                requiring players to determine the rules and logic behind each
                puzzle on their own.
              </p>

              <p>
                If you want to explore more puzzle hunts besides BayPHL, check
                out <a
                  href="https://puzzledpint.org/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer">Puzzled Pint</a
                >, <a
                  href="https://playdash.org/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer">DASH</a
                >, and the <a
                  href="https://puzzlehuntcalendar.com/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer">Puzzle Hunt Calendar</a
                >.
              </p>
            </Fragment>
          </FAQCard>

          <FAQCard>
            <Fragment slot="title">How is BayPHL different?</Fragment>
            <Fragment slot="content">
              Traditionally, BayPHL is built to incorporate specific physical
              locations, requiring teams to visit and explore sites in order to
              discover and solve puzzles.
            </Fragment>
          </FAQCard>

          <FAQCard>
            <Fragment slot="title">Who runs BayPHL?</Fragment>
            <Fragment slot="content">
              While there is a small team that coordinates and helps promote
              BayPHL events, there’s no one team that runs BayPHL. Each event is
              written and run by various groups of puzzle enthusiast volunteers
              from the Bay Area and beyond.
            </Fragment>
          </FAQCard>

          <FAQCard>
            <Fragment slot="title">Can I run a BayPHL?</Fragment>
            <Fragment slot="content">
              <p>
                Sure! We want to enable more Bay Area puzzle hunts. Not sure you
                want to write something new? We’re also happy to help you
                recreate old puzzle hunts from the Bay Area or elsewhere. Did
                you run a puzzle hunt 20 years ago that the kids these days
                might not know about?
              </p>

              <p>
                Let’s talk! Reach out to <a href="mailto:bayphl@bayphl.org"
                  >bayphl@bayphl.org</a
                >
              </p>
            </Fragment>
          </FAQCard>

          <FAQCard>
            <Fragment slot="title">How can I learn more?</Fragment>
            <Fragment slot="content">
              If you’re interested in learning about future BayPHL events, <a
                href="https://groups.google.com/g/bayphl-announce"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                subscribe to our announcement list
              </a> or <a
                href="https://bsky.app/profile/bayphl.org"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer">follow us on social media</a
              >
            </Fragment>
          </FAQCard>

          <FAQCard>
            <Fragment slot="title">Where did the name come from?</Fragment>
            <Fragment slot="content">
              Frankly, “BAPHL” might be a better name, but it was already taken
              by our friends at the <a href="https://baphl.org"
                >Boston Area Puzzle Hunt League</a
              >, so we needed some way to distinguish ourselves.
            </Fragment>
          </FAQCard>
        </FAQCardGrid>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
